# What the cross-toolchain images do not need in their build context.
#
# Neither Containerfile copies anything in - both are FROM plus RUN, and the
# source tree arrives at *run* time as a bind mount (-v "${PWD}:/src"). So the
# context should be close to empty, and was instead 1.4 GB of build output and
# Visual Studio index.
#
# That is not only slow. `.vs/` holds files VS keeps open, and podman failed
# outright trying to read one:
#
#     failed to close build request body: open .vs/.../*.vsidx:
#     The process cannot access the file because it is being used by
#     another process
#
# A build that cannot run while the IDE is open is a build nobody runs.

# Build output. Large, and regenerated by the build inside the container.
build/
out/

# Visual Studio and VS Code local state. `.vs/` is the one that locks files.
.vs/
.vscode/

# Git history. The image does not inspect the repository.
.git/

# Captured device images and probe reports. These carry a serial, an SSID and
# a MAC, and they have no business in an image layer even by accident.
restore/
device-probe.md

# Emulator and site output.
site/emulator/*.wasm
site/emulator/*.js
